From a6b00806dae05fedcffdf9d04beca2809f7a6384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][CEC] A line on which nothing answers is not opened by
 libCEC, and the waits of the adapter end when it stops

Issue 24 (report of 2026-11-20 20:15:50): after the PC woke at 20:03:45, the
CEC adapter of a DisplayPort output (DP-2) failed to open at 20:03:57, and
Kodi wrote nothing more of it until it ended at 20:06:16. The kernel log
says why: on that line every message "timed out" and every logical address
was "polling ... failed with tx_status=0x00a0" (timeout after the retries),
from Kodi's start on; libCEC claimed addresses, polled the TV and reported
itself over and over, and its second open did not return in two minutes.
Kodi did not try the adapter again meanwhile, and the end of Kodi waited
11 s for the thread of the adapter (StopThread()), as sleep would.

Before libCEC opens an adapter of the kernel, the line is asked once now:
a poll from the unregistered address to the TV (0xf0, which the kernel
sends on an adapter without a logical address), blocking. A result of the
line, an acknowledgement or a negative one, says that it works, and libCEC
opens it as before; a refused poll, or one aborted, says nothing, and so
does an adapter that has logical addresses (in use): libCEC opens it as
before. Two polls in a row with no result of the line (a timeout, an error,
lost arbitration) give it up: libCEC is not asked to open it, kodi.log says
so once, and it is asked again every 30 s, so that a line that comes alive
(a TV switched on, another cable) is opened then (CEC_LINE). The waits of
the thread of the adapter between attempts end when the thread is stopped,
at sleep or at the end of Kodi, instead of sleeping out their 10 s.
---
